  "notes": "Official cause code is TBD/provisional per FORM-366 fields; narrative attributes the trip to a mechanical/electrical connection failure (loose shorting screws) rather than assigning a formal cause code category. Two failure events are linked: the Aug 2, 2021 pump trip and the retroactively-discovered extended inoperability (Feb 1-Aug 4, 2021) traced to the same root cause via cause evaluation. EFW system itself served as its own backup via redundant trains (2A MDEFW and TDEFW pumps), which were stated operable throughout the inoperability window -- modeled via BACKED_UP_BY to sys_ba representing the redundant EFW train capability; individual redundant pump components (2A MDEFW, TDEFW) were not separately modeled as System nodes since the narrative treats them as alternate trains of the same EFW System already captured. Auxiliary Steam System [SB] and steam headers were mentioned only as EFW system design context (steam supply description) and were excluded from INVOLVES/edges per rule 6, though the System node is retained for completeness of EIIS mapping potential; no edges assert its involvement in the failure chain."
